{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op","id":1376957,"title":"Swarm form too OP?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-28T07:18:54-07:00","id":1376957,"title":"Swarm form too OP?","content":"How can a Gangrel in Swarm Form be handled. I mean, without flamethrower, granades, &quot;pesticides&quot;. It happened a frenzied Gangrel in my quest attacjed a BP 6 Elder, with tons of disciplines and it resulted in the Elder run away in front of a BP 3, relatively young vampire.<br /> <br /> In Swarm you are applying all your physical discipline and stats, ignoring defense and you just receive 1 (max 2) damages per attack. In frenzy you even cannot be affected from mental discipline.<br /> <br /> Also, with Claws of Unholy are you still supposed to deal aggravated whil in Swarm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T07:34:11-07:00","id":1376959,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can use claws of the unholy in swarm. because the swarm does not have claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T07:43:55-07:00","id":1376961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1376959#post1376959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can use claws of the unholy in swarm. because the swarm does not have claws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I thought the same but as the different transformations are actually stackable (read as, wolf from protean 3 + claws from protean 4) I'm not sure whz several bats, or rats cannot have thiny claws as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T09:25:03-07:00","id":1376972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op#post1376957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Gangrel in Swarm Form be handled. I mean, without flamethrower, granades, &quot;pesticides&quot;. It happened a frenzied Gangrel in my quest attacjed a BP 6 Elder, with tons of disciplines and it resulted in the Elder run away in front of a BP 3, relatively young vampire.<br /> <br /> In Swarm you are applying all your physical discipline and stats, ignoring defense and you just receive 1 (max 2) damages per attack. In frenzy you even cannot be affected from mental discipline.<br /> <br /> Also, with Claws of Unholy are you still supposed to deal aggravated whil in Swarm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ya Swarm Form is a tough combo, especially against another Vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T09:29:22-07:00","id":1376974,"title":"","content":"I guess it would then rely on the storyteller to approve that. While rats and bats have claws to a normal human they wouldn't be able to do the damage that a tiger's claws could do. So personally I would say no to Claws of the Unholy in swarm form. I would also say that the swarm loses the toughness of a vampire as in Lethal damage and not be downgraded to bashing. the vampire still gets other armor(though even then I would say that they would lose everything except resilience armor due to being transformed.) Though that is just my reading of the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 03-28-2020, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T18:58:10-07:00","id":1377039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op#post1376957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Gangrel in Swarm Form be handled. I mean, without flamethrower, granades, &quot;pesticides&quot;. It happened a frenzied Gangrel in my quest attacjed a BP 6 Elder, with tons of disciplines and it resulted in the Elder run away in front of a BP 3, relatively young vampire.<br /> <br /> In Swarm you are applying all your physical discipline and stats, ignoring defense and you just receive 1 (max 2) damages per attack. In frenzy you even cannot be affected from mental discipline.<br /> <br /> Also, with Claws of Unholy are you still supposed to deal aggravated whil in Swarm?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Swarms can only damage those caught inside it\u2019s radius. Instead of standing still like an idiot and allowing yourself to be swarmed, use your movement to move beyond its radius. Any stragglers and hanger ons that are moved beyond the swarm radius immediately shrivel and die, reducing the swarm size accordingly. <br /> <br /> Spilling a glass of water should disperse a large part of the swarm. Tossing a Solo cup of beer or glass of wine and dropping a match should be more than sufficient to destroy a large chunk of the swarm or kill it. Alcohol is quick burning and likely to be consumed before potentially igniting anything else. Ditto for igniting a napkin or handkerchief and tossing it at the swarm. <br /> <br /> A fire extinguisher, leaf blower, or power washer also works for quickly dispersing a swarm form into piles of vermin corpses. Imagine being the Gangrel getting his ass beat into torpor by someone with a vacuum cleaner. <br /> <br /> <br /> By the way Swarm Form and Claws of the Unholy are both merits, so no they are not stackable. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T19:01:57-07:00","id":1377041,"title":"","content":"Also can you be in frenzy and be in swarm form at the same time? I guess it is possible but I would think being in frenzy would kick the vampire out of swarm form as the beast wouldn't be able to hold unto the many different minds it has to control and would put you back into human form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T20:14:56-07:00","id":1377051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1376959#post1376959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you can use claws of the unholy in swarm. because the swarm does not have claws.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they kinda do. Lots of them, but they are tiny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T03:14:10-07:00","id":1377142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377039#post1377039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Swarms can only damage those caught inside it\u2019s radius. Instead of standing still like an idiot and allowing yourself to be swarmed, use your movement to move beyond its radius. Any stragglers and hanger ons that are moved beyond the swarm radius immediately shrivel and die, reducing the swarm size accordingly.<br /> <br /> Spilling a glass of water should disperse a large part of the swarm. Tossing a Solo cup of beer or glass of wine and dropping a match should be more than sufficient to destroy a large chunk of the swarm or kill it. Alcohol is quick burning and likely to be consumed before potentially igniting anything else. Ditto for igniting a napkin or handkerchief and tossing it at the swarm.<br /> <br /> A fire extinguisher, leaf blower, or power washer also works for quickly dispersing a swarm form into piles of vermin corpses. Imagine being the Gangrel getting his ass beat into torpor by someone with a vacuum cleaner.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way Swarm Form and Claws of the Unholy are both merits, so no they are not stackable.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm lost. I've never said the vampire has to stay still in the swarm as I've written he had to ran away indeed.<br /> Moving outside the radius will not spare you for the next turn. It's not a chess game where you are moving, then your opponent is moving. Movment come at almost the same time (reasonably) so if the elder move away at up his speed meeter, the swarm can do the same following him to be ready to attack the very next turn unless the elder do not use celerity if he has it higher than the Vampire in swarm form (as you are allowed to use all your discipline while in swarm). So moving away, if not to escape, doesn't really make any difference.<br /> <br /> Why spilling a glass of whater should disperse the swarm? A vampire in Swarm Form is still using the vampire skills and attributes (I even can't see how a glass of whater could disperse a normal swarm summoned with Animalism 3...). Any area attack will simply deal the total amount of damage, but whether the vampire has resilence, or enough health point, it doesn imply he will be dispersed for sure. by the way, using fires, flamethrowers, granade it's for sure useful but no every elder is going around with them in the pocket.<br /> <br /> I can't see how a vacuum (wich could be useful while in fog form indeed), can be useful against a flock of crows or a herd of rat. Fire extinguisher will for sure have some advantage in this scenario, like giving the swarm distracted condition, but not more.<br /> <br /> When you say merits are not stackable where did you get this info? So I can't use Boxing style and Defensive combat in the same turn? It sounds weird....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377041#post1377041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also can you be in frenzy and be in swarm form at the same time? I guess it is possible but I would think being in frenzy would kick the vampire out of swarm form as the beast wouldn't be able to hold unto the many different minds it has to control and would put you back into human form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you definitely can. You do not have any different mind but just one as specified in the book. All the swarm is moving under a unique mind and it cannot even spread to wide...so no dispersion at all. Swarm form is still an unique being (I guess Dracula untold style pretty much).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377051#post1377051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they kinda do. Lots of them, but they are tiny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, same way they have tiny teeth but they are specified to still deal the Vampire full damage, so I guess the number compensate the size.<br /> <br /> Swarm form is also having the very same strenght of the vampire... is just having the following benefit:<br /> <br /> 1. Suffering only one (max 2) damage per turn if not from any area attack<br /> 2. ignoring defense<br /> 3. using the vampire pools<br /> 4. inflicting distracted condition<br /> 5. can only steal 1 vitae per turn<br /> <br /> no other advantages or disvantages so I guess we should stick with all other rules applicable if not for any houserule of yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-29-2020, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T08:00:26-07:00","id":1377176,"title":"","content":"So my reading of the rules for swarm is that the attack the swarm does is a bite attack of some sort by evidence of the can steal one point of vitae. And yes you can be kinda be affected by mental powers in frenzy. the example in the book states that you can be dominated to attack a different target and I assume it can work in other ways as well. using majesty to convince the frenzy vampire into turning on its friends because they were the one to insult the vampire and not the elder. Also the swarms speed is adjusted for the size of the creature the vampire becomes. so if you become a size one rat swarm you are losing at least four points of speed, a size zero bug losing five. so unless this is a elder in name only he should be able to move out of the effective range of the swarm and still be able to effect it in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T10:15:26-07:00","id":1377194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377176#post1377176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my reading of the rules for swarm is that the attack the swarm does is a bite attack of some sort by evidence of the can steal one point of vitae. And yes you can be kinda be affected by mental powers in frenzy. the example in the book states that you can be dominated to attack a different target and I assume it can work in other ways as well. using majesty to convince the frenzy vampire into turning on its friends because they were the one to insult the vampire and not the elder. Also the swarms speed is adjusted for the size of the creature the vampire becomes. so if you become a size one rat swarm you are losing at least four points of speed, a size zero bug losing five. so unless this is a elder in name only he should be able to move out of the effective range of the swarm and still be able to effect it in other ways.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Swarm form allow you to, instead taking the shape of only ONE bat/rat/crow, to multiply that shape in a multitude. Why they should be able to use only the bite and no any other means they could use in a single being is a mystery. The eveidence of taking vitae is not an evidence at all as it is written: &quot;alternately a success may INSTEAD allow to take one vitae&quot;. Evidence that the atttack is not mandatory to be by theeth at all as it is just an alternative.<br /> <br /> About mental disciplines, yes, you can ONLY deviate the target, if another target is there, otherwise you can't deviate it. It0s specified you cannot change the Freny purpose, only the target. No other target means it is not possible, but again, this is not what I wanted to discuss about. The elder escaped saving his life. I was just considering that, as the power is written, an Elder with high physical disciplines/attributes, can't do that much against a relatively young kindred in swarm form. <br /> <br /> About swarm speed, yes, the species factor is adjusted, and it can also be increased indeed as a bat, for example, has specie factor 10, which means even faster than before.<br /> <br /> And again, yes an elder could be able to move out and run away, which was my point at the very first post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T11:37:43-07:00","id":1377203,"title":"","content":"Maybe it can't be fixed. so if you are the storyteller there is ways for that elder to punish that young vampire for embarrassing them. sending people around to fire bomb their haven or getting a bunch of other people to attack the other vampire, use other mental powers to control them, try to force them into a blood bond. so make some house rules if you think its too powerful. no one says you have to play RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 03-29-2020, 02:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T18:09:13-07:00","id":1377251,"title":"","content":"Swarm form is quite powerful but remember it DOES cost 5xp for both the Discipline and the Merit so he could almost get another level of Discipline instead.<br /> <br /> That being said, you as the ST do have one powerful tool at your disposal: It is an animal form, and when a Vampire uses Protean*** pg140 to transform, they take on the statistics of that animal(s). There are suggestions in a couple places for swarm stats but ultimately you as the ST get to stat it out. Strength, Stamina/HP, Speed, and Brawl will be the major ones to tweak the power level. Low Stamina/HP and he's still tough, probably tougher than normal form, but low HP will make him more vulnerable while low Str &amp; Brawl will limit his offensive power and the only way he can raise these is by investing in physical Disciplines. Low speed means maybe he can take on anyone who chooses to try and fight but he doesn't get a vote on when or where the fight occurs, nor can he escape if things go sideways.<br /> <br /> I don't know why Merits wouldn't stack because I don't recall seeing that as a thing anywhere so as for Claws of the Unholy (which requires Protean FOUR), you could build in consequences to such a reckless action as purposely flying into a frenzy. Perhaps the targets takes a bystander, loved one, or coterie member as a human shield or just tosses them in front of himself and the swarm rips them to pieces to get through. Perhaps the target flees out into public and the swarm causes a Masquerade breach. Perhaps the target realizes that he's frenzied and lures the swarm into a hazard that ignores it's resilience to damage such as exposed electrical wires or something.<br /> <br /> Also things that damage Willpower or drain Vitae are unaffected by the resilience of the swam, so that's another avenue of attack.<br /> <br /> If bats are his thing then something as simple as a stout bedsheet can completely ruin his career. Perhaps a loud TV or radio in the room could screw up echolocation or even cause damage to sensitive ears. Lure the swarm into another room and slam the door on the other half of the swarm, and if he continues to follow, then half the creatures will automatically die off (and lose half his HP?) when they get out of range from the rest.<br /> <br /> Also the thing with Gangrel is that eventually they can become the Unstoppable Force and the Immovable Object so you could engineer constant low-grade threats to other things to which he is attached. If he goes the combat wombat route then he can only be in one place at a time and the harder he commits, the less he can protect something else like Haven(s), Touchestone(s), Contacts, Allies, etc. If he's pissed off an Elder then I would expect the Elder to go that route anyway and avoid personal combat.<br /> <br /> Just remember that it costs minimum of 11 xp for Protean 3 + Swarm form, and 15 xp for P4 + Claws of the Unholy so It should be powerful but hopefully there's something here that can stop it from breaking your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-29-2020, 09:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-29T19:19:41-07:00","id":1377260,"title":"","content":"Swarm Form specifically uses the vampire's own stats, not that of the animal.<br /> <br /> Merits do stack, but Claws of the Unholy is honestly overrated. Most people don't wear any armour so that part is highly situational, on top of dealing less damage and not being useful for incapacitating people (as opposed to outright killing them).<br /> The only part I think is worth to XP cost is that the opponent can't heal it in the middle of combat, but a proper elder should have a bunch of Resilience to block [dots+1] damage and downgrade [dots] damage to healable lethal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T02:28:58-07:00","id":1377316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377260#post1377260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm Form specifically uses the vampire's own stats, not that of the animal.<br /> <br /> Merits do stack, but Claws of the Unholy is honestly overrated. Most people don't wear any armour so that part is highly situational, on top of dealing less damage and not being useful for incapacitating people (as opposed to outright killing them).<br /> The only part I think is worth to XP cost is that the opponent can't heal it in the middle of combat, but a proper elder should have a bunch of Resilience to block [dots+1] damage and downgrade [dots] damage to healable lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree on everything.<br /> Maybe not too much about claws though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Yes it's lowering the damage but dealing aggravated which against any supernatural with regeneration (thinking about werewolves, vampires), it's key for victory. Also it's allowing you ti ingore durability, not just armor, which means you could potentially destroy the door of a caveau.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T12:48:01-07:00","id":1377384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377260#post1377260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Swarm Form specifically uses the vampire's own stats, not that of the animal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a fine house rule but according to RAW you use Beast's Skin, then apply a few modifiers, none of which are &quot;Use the Vampire's own Physical Attributes and Skills instead.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T16:12:25-07:00","id":1377405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377384#post1377384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a fine house rule but according to RAW you use Beast's Skin, then apply a few modifiers, none of which are &quot;Use the Vampire's own Physical Attributes and Skills instead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> according to RAW: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those inside. </div> </div> </div>What strenght+Brawl are they talking abou if there is no swarm stat defined in the book? The strenght+brawl of a single animal of that kind? So in the case of a size 0 animal (like a bug) should I roll 0? Does not make sense to me rolling 0 dice as if a bat has strenght 1 I guess a bug has strenght and brawl 0.<br /> <br /> For me the text is referring to the Vampire Strenght+Brawl. <br /> <br /> You use beast's skin but the Swarm form is working differently. FIrst of all it allow you to become a swarm of size 0 creatures while that's not the case for Beast's skin.<br /> If you argue about the text of sawrm form is not specyfing Vampire Strenght + Brawl, it's not even specyfing it's the animal pool. Which does not make sense in case of size 0 animals and definitely not any sense at all even for size 1 animals. (dividing the amount of damage however you wiush among those inside, also, with a pool of 2 means pretty much dividing 1 damage if you are lucky...).<br /> <br /> If you think it was the developer's intention, I honestly hope it wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T17:15:31-07:00","id":1377410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377384#post1377384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fine house rule but according to RAW you use Beast's Skin, then apply a few modifiers, none of which are &quot;Use the Vampire's own Physical Attributes and Skills instead.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, you use the rules written under Swarm Form when you use Swarm Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T17:25:00-07:00","id":1377412,"title":"","content":"Yeah, got to agree with Rathamus here. no where in the swarm form rules does it say use the the vampire stats. only their speed adjusted for the size of they choose. so you would have to come up with some swarm form stats. just like everything else you would use Beast's Skin for. so one could fix it by working with the storyteller and coming to agreement on a stat block that you could use for swarm.<br /> <br /> Rules for swarm form.<br /> <br /> Effect: When taking the Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can<br /> instead become a swarm of small creatures: Size 0 or Size 1<br /> animals. The character may perceive through any of the senses<br /> of any individual creature in the swarm, but the swarm acts as<br /> a single entity.<br /> The swarm may spread over five yards or meters per dot of<br /> Blood Potency. Creatures beyond that range die and rapidly<br /> decompose. The swarm moves at the vampire\u2019s Speed, modified<br /> for the creatures\u2019 Size, in any logical direction.<br /> The swarm limits visibility and hearing, and causes panic in<br /> all those present. Everyone within the swarm\u2019s area suffers the<br /> persistent Distracted Condition (see p.302) until they get away.<br /> With Storyteller discretion, a swarm may have other features<br /> suited to the swarm animal. For example, rats should be better<br /> at biting through barricades.<br /> The swarm resists most harm. Roll attacks against the swarm<br /> as normal, but after factoring armor and other modifiers, the<br /> swarm only takes one point of damage of the appropriate type at<br /> most, or two points of damage with an exceptional success. Fire,<br /> sunlight, explosions, and other large-scale threats cause normal<br /> harm to the swarm, which is affected by banes as normal. To<br /> attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring<br /> Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those<br /> inside. Apply a victim\u2019s armor to the damage normally. The<br /> damage is lethal (bashing to Kindred). Alternately, a success<br /> may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 03-30-2020, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-30T17:41:15-07:00","id":1377414,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377410#post1377410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By RAW, you use the rules written under Swarm Form when you use Swarm Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed and the <u><i>very first</i></u> sentence for Swarm Form is: &quot;When taking the Beast's Skin...&quot; Later on when they reference &quot;Roll Strength + Brawl&quot; they are referring to the stats of the swarm because that is the baseline of this power. There actually is one place where they specifically note to use the Vampire's own stats, and that is in reference to movement speed. Why would they specifically call out that one specific part unless the intent was for the rest of the power to behave in the same way as Beast's Skin as stated in the very first sentence?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377405#post1377405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What strenght+Brawl are they talking abou if there is no swarm stat defined in the book? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Where do they have stats for other animal forms? There are some in a word file here on the forum but also the ChroD base book which also includes a templates for various animals and antagonists, one of which is &quot;swarm of vermin&quot;. I personally think that template is on the strong side but you as the ST get to make of it what you will.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if you decided to stat it out yourself, a starting point could be to take the base animal's stats and bump strength and stamina by a dot or two for the extra muscle and biomass, then bump brawl by maybe a couple dots to signify swarm tactic coordination or something. Most size zero creatures are going to be quite low in all of those stats so you're looking at 2-3 dots each.<br /> <br /> Again I think using the Vampire's stats is a just peachy homebrew rule if you like that, but a thorough read of the actual wording makes it clear that by RAW you use the &quot;Physical Attributes and Skills&quot; of the swarm.<br /> <br /> Edit: It is also clear why they would word it in this way to prevent it from becoming overpowered. If it used the Vampire's own stats then they could easily break the power by spending xp on physical attributes and skills to steadily increase the combat effectiveness of the swarm. By making it use the animal's stats, they are forever fixed in place and even physical Disciplines are hardcapped at 5 dots whereas attributes can go all the way up to 10 with higher Blood Potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 03-30-2020, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T00:46:22-07:00","id":1377469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377414#post1377414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Indeed and the <u><i>very first</i></u> sentence for Swarm Form is: &quot;When taking the Beast's Skin...&quot; Later on when they reference &quot;Roll Strength + Brawl&quot; they are referring to the stats of the swarm because that is the baseline of this power. There actually is one place where they specifically note to use the Vampire's own stats, and that is in reference to movement speed. Why would they specifically call out that one specific part unless the intent was for the rest of the power to behave in the same way as Beast's Skin as stated in the very first sentence?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Where do they have stats for other animal forms? There are some in a word file here on the forum but also the ChroD base book which also includes a templates for various animals and antagonists, one of which is &quot;swarm of vermin&quot;. I personally think that template is on the strong side but you as the ST get to make of it what you will.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if you decided to stat it out yourself, a starting point could be to take the base animal's stats and bump strength and stamina by a dot or two for the extra muscle and biomass, then bump brawl by maybe a couple dots to signify swarm tactic coordination or something. Most size zero creatures are going to be quite low in all of those stats so you're looking at 2-3 dots each.<br /> <br /> Again I think using the Vampire's stats is a just peachy homebrew rule if you like that, but a thorough read of the actual wording makes it clear that by RAW you use the &quot;Physical Attributes and Skills&quot; of the swarm.<br /> <br /> Edit: It is also clear why they would word it in this way to prevent it from becoming overpowered. If it used the Vampire's own stats then they could easily break the power by spending xp on physical attributes and skills to steadily increase the combat effectiveness of the swarm. By making it use the animal's stats, they are forever fixed in place and even physical Disciplines are hardcapped at 5 dots whereas attributes can go all the way up to 10 with higher Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. They slecifically call on the part of &quot;when taking beast's form&quot; because Swarm form is applying only if you have beast's form and only after having paid the Beast's form cost. Same way as Protean 4 is applying on protean 2 and it say: when acquising transformation from protean 2...<br /> <br /> 2. Swarm form is also allowing you to become a swarm of size 0 animals which is not the case for beast's form itself, hence you are actually becoming a different animal than your original transformation<br /> <br /> 3. Here (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...FVgSqjmpo/edit</a>) is the word doc with animal stat which is not including any swarm template. I went through CoD book and I couldn't find any swarm template as well. Pls point us out where the stats for sucg swarm are. So far, for me they aren't anywhere, hence the book cannot refer to any of such strenght+brawl roll of such<br /> <br /> 4. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377414#post1377414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Perhaps if you decided to stat it out yourself, a starting point could be to take the base animal's stats and bump strength and stamina by a dot or two for the extra muscle and biomass, then bump brawl by maybe a couple dots to signify swarm tactic coordination or something.</div> </div> </div> </div> which it's definitely a house rule which we are not discussing about at this point.<br /> <br /> 5. Again, the book is clearily saying: to attack those whithin the swarm, roll Strenght+brawl, ignoring defense. As you are using Vampire speed (yes, modified for the size - which for me should be written species factor - of that kind of animals), I do not see any reason to use this stat for the speed and another, unwritten, stat for the attack roll. As a funny coincidence Speed is calculated as Strenght+Dexterity+Species factor which, in my opinion, it's another confirmation you should use Vampire stats. Otherwise it make totally no sense for me. But if you could point me out any swarm Strenght + Brawl stat, I can see, somehow, your point. Even if still not agreeing because of all the points above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377414#post1377414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Edit: It is also clear why they would word it in this way to prevent it from becoming overpowered. If it used the Vampire's own stats then they could easily break the power by spending xp on physical attributes and skills to steadily increase the combat effectiveness of the swarm. By making it use the animal's stats, they are forever fixed in place and even physical Disciplines are hardcapped at 5 dots whereas attributes can go all the way up to 10 with higher Blood Potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>which indeed you can as you can boost your stat with blood and vigor, also while in basic Beast's skin form.... <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While in animal form, the vampire can use her disciplines as noormal </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-31-2020, 04:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T04:32:29-07:00","id":1377488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377469#post1377469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. They slecifically call on the part of &quot;when taking beast's form&quot; because Swarm form is applying only if you have beast's form and only after having paid the Beast's form cost. Same way as Protean 4 is applying on protean 2 and it say: when acquising transformation from protean 2...<br /> <br /> 2. Swarm form is also allowing you to become a swarm of size 0 animals which is not the case for beast's form itself, hence you are actually becoming a different animal than your original transformation<br /> <br /> 3. Here (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...FVgSqjmpo/edit</a>) is the word doc with animal stat which is not including any swarm template. I went through CoD book and I couldn't find any swarm template as well. Pls point us out where the stats for sucg swarm are. So far, for me they aren't anywhere, hence the book cannot refer to any of such strenght+brawl roll of such<br /> <br /> 4. which it's definitely a house rule which we are not discussing about at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> which indeed you can as you can boost your stat with blood and vigor, also while in basic Beast's skin form....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 1 &amp; 2. I think you just made my point for me. Yes you take on the form of a beast and Swarm Form expands your options to include a swarm of size 0 or 1 animals. It does not say to entirely revamp the mechanics for that except where otherwise noted.<br /> <br /> 3. As mentioned above, the Chronicles of Darkness book on page 121 contains a sample stat block which includes &quot;swarm of vermin.&quot; You can open the pdf and presst Ctl-F then just type &quot;swarm of vermin&quot; to find it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T05:14:45-07:00","id":1377497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377488#post1377488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1 &amp; 2. I think you just made my point for me. Yes you take on the form of a beast and Swarm Form expands your options to include a swarm of size 0 or 1 animals. It does not say to entirely revamp the mechanics for that except where otherwise noted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you can read it in your favor if you like while it is not. It is not supposed to say: completely revamp the mechanics as it not not even saying use animal swarm stats. It is ONLY saying, as Swarm Form is a merit which is empowering a discipline, &quot;<i>when taking the Beast's Skin, some Gangrel can INSTEAD, become a swarm...&quot;. </i>Whether we are analysing word by word, which is quite useless, INSTEAD can be read as AN ALTERNATIVE OF Beast's Skin. Which is not where I want to go through. As, for me, it is simply saying: You can become a Swarm when you activate Beast's Skin as, without having this specification, anyone else with this merit and Protean 3, could become a Swarm at no cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377488#post1377488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. As mentioned above, the Chronicles of Darkness book on page 121 contains a sample stat block which includes &quot;swarm of vermin.&quot; You can open the pdf and presst Ctl-F then just type &quot;swarm of vermin&quot; to find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, I have the CoD book open in front of me, I already looked for Swarm of vermin and I was only redirected to a power with no stat, suggesting that with this you can command or become a Vermin Swarm. Then, as you suggested, I went directly to page 121 and no stat of this Swarm. Maybe I have another version I don't know. But I can't find any block stat for any kind of swarm.<br /> <br /> At page 121 I just have: Possessed Demon Cultist, Slick professional Grifter, Trained Guard Dog (which under Double as it has Swarm of vermin - with no stat), World Weary private eye. Looking in the whole Antagonist section I still cannot find Swarm of vermin stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-31-2020, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:21:01-07:00","id":1377505,"title":"","content":"Double means that you can use the trained guard dog stats to represent a swarm of vermin.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that was published a long time after Swarm Form was published, not to mention that each game is supposed to be fully playable without additional supplements. That list of animals was specifically made to complement Vampire.<br /> <br /> Neither can we use the animal's own stat in many cases because most animals with Size 0 would never be represented through stats. An ant does not have any Attribute or Skill dots, or any derived Traits. It's simply a feature of the environment.<br /> <br /> By process of elimination, it's only the vampire's own stats that can be used in those cases. For the sake of consistency they should be used in all cases.<br /> <br /> Then there's also the matter of &quot;does this make sense?&quot; Does it make sense that several cubic meters of vermin all tearing at a victim would be just as effective as a single individual in terms of the dice pool? While also dealing lethal damage even if the species (like toads, or most insects) naturally deals bashing?<br /> Does it make more sense that the swarm is a physical representation of the vampire and uses the vampire's stats, rather than those of a single individual creature within the swarm with no scaling to account for the fact that it's a swarm?<br /> I think the latter makes much more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:31:39-07:00","id":1377506,"title":"","content":"Totally agreeing with Tessie. There is really no evidence that the players should figure out any kind of swarm stats from nowhere while it's clearily stated: use strenght+brawl. I cannot even see how a swarm can have a skill like brawl not being a unique identity (a part of this specific case as it is the vampire representation).<br /> <br /> The only other swarm rule which I'm actually using to deal with animalism 3, is the one presented in the Demon sourcebook. Which, indeed, has no stats but just automatc (bashing) damage each turn. And I don't think, anyway, Requiem core book is referencing or should even refer to another splat manual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 03-31-2020, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T11:52:33-07:00","id":1377545,"title":"","content":"Applying the normal Beast\u2019s Skin stat changes would mean you have the same Health as a swarm of rats that you\u2019d have as a single rat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T16:46:46-07:00","id":1377816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377506#post1377506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Totally agreeing with Tessie. There is really no evidence that the players should figure out any kind of swarm stats from nowhere while it's clearily stated: use strenght+brawl. I cannot even see how a swarm can have a skill like brawl not being a unique identity (a part of this specific case as it is the vampire representation).</div> </div> </div> </div>So if you transform into a rabbit, then what stats do you use to attack? Would it usually be strength+brawl? Would you assume to use the vampires base-form stats because there are no rabbit stats in the book? If not then why assume such a thing for swarm form?<br /> <br /> TRAINED<br /> GUARD DOG<br /> \u201c*bark! bark!* Grrrrr...\u201d<br /> Description: It\u2019s a Doberman Pinscher, a Rottweiler,<br /> or a German Shepherd. Its teeth are bared and its ears are<br /> pointed at you. You\u2019re in its territory and it plans to rip you<br /> to pieces with all its friends. It can track you wherever you<br /> run, and it\u2019s faster than you.<br /> Attributes: Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 3,<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Presence 3,<br /> Manipulation 0, Composure 1<br /> General Dice Pools: Born Survivor 7, Marathon<br /> Runner 7, Aggressive Growl 5<br /> Combat Dice Pools: Bite 6, Tackle 6<br /> Initiative Modifier: +5<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 0<br /> Size: 4<br /> Speed: 12<br /> <b>Doubles as</b>: K-9 hound, wild animal, <u><b>swarm of<br /> vermin</b></u>, genetic experiment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Doubles as&quot; means that you can substitute the name and it's basically the same thing. If you have frogs then just change the dice pool from marathon runner to hopping or whatever floats your boat.<br /> <br /> Tessie is correct that the ChroD book was printed well after the VTR book so swarm form was already well established and well known for the writers to take into account.<br /> If the VTR book were fully capable of being used on it's own then why does it not include stats for a dog, frog, raven, etc? That logic does not add up at all. If you are looking for an OFFICIAL, printed stat block for a &quot;swarm of vermin,&quot; then that is presented in the ChroD book.<br /> <br /> Again, one cool thing about TT games is that you are free to homebrew however you please. The plain English reading of this specific power though, does not say what are assuming it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-01-2020, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T17:00:22-07:00","id":1377822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377816#post1377816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if you transform into a dog, then what stats do you use to attack? Would it usually be strength+brawl? Would you assume to use the vampires base-form stats because there are no dog stats in the VTR book? If not then why assume such a thing for swarm form?<br /> <br /> If the book were fully capable of being used on it's own then why does it not include stats for a dog, frog, raven, etc? That logic does not add up at all. If you are looking for an OFFICIAL, printed stat block for a &quot;swarm of vermin,&quot; then that is presented in the ChroD book.<br /> <br /> Again, one cool thing about TT games is that you are free to homebrew however you please. The plain English reading of this specific power though, does not work the way you are assuming it does.<br /> <br /> <br /> TRAINED<br /> GUARD DOG<br /> \u201c*bark! bark!* Grrrrr...\u201d<br /> Description: It\u2019s a Doberman Pinscher, a Rottweiler,<br /> or a German Shepherd. Its teeth are bared and its ears are<br /> pointed at you. You\u2019re in its territory and it plans to rip you<br /> to pieces with all its friends. It can track you wherever you<br /> run, and it\u2019s faster than you.<br /> Attributes: Intelligence 1, Wits 4, Resolve 3,<br /> Strength 4, Dexterity 4, Stamina 3, Presence 3,<br /> Manipulation 0, Composure 1<br /> General Dice Pools: Born Survivor 7, Marathon<br /> Runner 7, Aggressive Growl 5<br /> Combat Dice Pools: Bite 6, Tackle 6<br /> Initiative Modifier: +5<br /> Defense: 7<br /> Health: 7<br /> Willpower: 0<br /> Size: 4<br /> Speed: 12<br /> <u><b>Doubles as</b></u>: K-9 hound, wild animal, <u><b>swarm of<br /> vermin</b></u>, genetic experiment.<br /> <br /> &quot;Doubles as&quot; means that you can substitute the name and it's basically the same thing. If you have frogs then just change the dice pool from marathon runner to hopping or whatever floats your boat.<br /> I also already addressed a simple and logical way to stat out a swarm if you don't like the stats presented on the officially published chrod book, and Tessie is correct that it was printed well after the VTR book so swarm form was already well established and well known for the writers to take into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast's skin is specyfing to use physical attributes and skills of the animal while mental from the vampire, swarm form is not.<br /> <br /> Anyway, seems we are in an impasse. I can't see any reason to change my mind, and I tried as I am of the idea that swarm form is bit op. I can house rule it but I'm still thinking my interpretation is right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-02-2020, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:43:08-07:00","id":1377852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377822#post1377822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast's skin is specyfing to use physical attributes and skills of the animal while mental from the vampire, swarm form is not.<br /> <br /> Anyway, seems we are in an impasse. I can't see any reason to take change my mind, and I tried as I am of the idea that swarm form is bit op. I can house rule it but I'm still thinking my interpretation is right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But no where does it say use anything else. It does not say substitute a vampire physical stats. You have to use Beast's skin to use swarm form. its why you have to have protean 3 to get the merit because you can't use swarm from without first using Beast's Skin. It says that in the write up for swarm form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T18:56:37-07:00","id":1377855,"title":"","content":"Cross-posted from the &quot;Vampires vs. Werewolves!&quot; thread: <br /> <br /> On swarms: as much as I like the VtR:2nd corebook, I'd suggest that Onyx Path really nailed the mechanics of swarms more effectively in Demon (pg. 179) and in Beast (pg. 126). If I were running another Vampire game, I'd probably adapt Swarm Form to the following:<br /> <br /> - Radius is two yards per dot of Blood Potency<br /> - Speed is double normal; move in three dimensions; fit through any opening<br /> - Inflict one bashing damage per turn to everything in the swarm's radius OR condense on one target &amp; inflict lethal damage/drain Vitae equal to Blood Potency<br /> - Armor effective against swarm damage only if covering the whole body, and even then only at half normal rating<br /> - Everyone else in the swarm's radius takes -2 penalty to all actions; may trigger Breaking Points for the entophobic<br /> - Taking damage reduces radius proportionally (take half damage, shrink to half size)<br /> - Non-area damage capped at 1 (normal) or 2 (Exceptional Success)<br /> - On any turn in which the swarm condenses, these caps double (max. 2 normal, 4 Exceptional); easier to squish a lot of tiny things when they're all tightly grouped together<br /> - Full damage from fire, sunlight, area attacks<br /> - Celerity &amp; Resilience work as normal<br /> - Vigor passive adds one yard of extra radius per dot; Vigor active adds to effective Blood Potency for that turn when condensing<br /> - Can't use Claws of the Unholy<br /> - Only one physical &quot;active&quot; effect per turn (<i>e.g.</i> if using Vigor active, can't use Celerity active)*<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> *Watsonian explanation: each of those tiny, gnashing bodies can't channel the power of the Curse as effectively as the vampire's &quot;real&quot; form, and/or the vampire's power is already taxed by independently coordinating so many moving parts at once.<br /> <br /> Doylist explanation: being a swarm already makes it very tough for most foes to cause you harm. It should be an overall buff, to reflect the XP spent on the Merit, but the combination of automatic lethal damage (Vigor active) + swarm immunity + preemption in case someone brought a grenade or a flamethrower (Celerity active) seems too much; pick two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-01T19:32:57-07:00","id":1377862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377855#post1377855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-posted from the &amp;quot;Vampires vs. Werewolves!&amp;quot; thread: <br /> <br /> On swarms: as much as I like the VtR:2nd corebook, I'd suggest that Onyx Path really nailed the mechanics of swarms more effectively in Demon (pg. 179) and in Beast (pg. 126). If I were running another Vampire game, I'd probably adapt Swarm Form to the following:<br /> <br /> - Radius is two yards per dot of Blood Potency<br /> - Speed is double normal; move in three dimensions; fit through any opening<br /> - Inflict one bashing damage per turn to everything in the swarm's radius OR condense on one target &amp; inflict lethal damage/drain Vitae equal to Blood Potency<br /> - Armor effective against swarm damage only if covering the whole body, and even then only at half normal rating<br /> - Everyone else in the swarm's radius takes -2 penalty to all actions; may trigger Breaking Points for the entophobic<br /> - Taking damage reduces radius proportionally (take half damage, shrink to half size)<br /> - Non-area damage capped at 1 (normal) or 2 (Exceptional Success)<br /> - On any turn in which the swarm condenses, these caps double (max. 2 normal, 4 Exceptional); easier to squish a lot of tiny things when they're all tightly grouped together<br /> - Full damage from fire, sunlight, area attacks<br /> - Celerity &amp; Resilience work as normal<br /> - Vigor passive adds one yard of extra radius per dot; Vigor active adds to effective Blood Potency for that turn when condensing<br /> - Can't use Claws of the Unholy<br /> - Only one physical &amp;quot;active&amp;quot; effect per turn (<i>e.g.</i> if using Vigor active, can't use Celerity active)*<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> *Watsonian explanation: each of those tiny, gnashing bodies can't channel the power of the Curse as effectively as the vampire's &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; form, and/or the vampire's power is already taxed by independently coordinating so many moving parts at once.<br /> <br /> Doylist explanation: being a swarm already makes it very tough for most foes to cause you harm. It should be an overall buff, to reflect the XP spent on the Merit, but the combination of automatic lethal damage (Vigor active) + swarm immunity + preemption in case someone brought a grenade or a flamethrower (Celerity active) seems too much; pick two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nice write up!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T01:02:55-07:00","id":1377899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377852#post1377852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But no where does it say use anything else. It does not say substitute a vampire physical stats. You have to use Beast's skin to use swarm form. its why you have to have protean 3 to get the merit because you can't use swarm from without first using Beast's Skin. It says that in the write up for swarm form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Swarm form says:<br /> <br /> 1. Use vampire speed scaled for size. Speed is Strenght + Dext + size. Without no reason then you are suggesting that: when it says: to attack use strenght+brawl, it is now strenght+brawl of a swarm.... Ok. Go for it.<br /> 2. AGAIN. You definitely need to have the basic discipline power cause the merit is just upgrading it. The merit is specifying: when using Beast's skin you can INSTEAD.... Beacause, otherwise, anyone with the prerequisite protean 3 and the merit could feel himself legitimate to become a swarm without speding the discipline vitae cost...but again, go for whatever you read the power.<br /> Use the speed from the vampire stat, then the strenght for brawling from a source written years after the Swarm Form merit, then the health from another source at your will. As long as you feel it good it's ok.<br /> <br /> I honestly do not have other arguments so I'm repeating the same all over this topic. If I have not coivinced you before I won't later. I step back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-02-2020, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T01:09:56-07:00","id":1377900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377855#post1377855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-posted from the &amp;quot;Vampires vs. Werewolves!&amp;quot; thread: <br /> <br /> On swarms: as much as I like the VtR:2nd corebook, I'd suggest that Onyx Path really nailed the mechanics of swarms more effectively in Demon (pg. 179) and in Beast (pg. 126). If I were running another Vampire game, I'd probably adapt Swarm Form to the following:<br /> <br /> - Radius is two yards per dot of Blood Potency<br /> - Speed is double normal; move in three dimensions; fit through any opening<br /> - Inflict one bashing damage per turn to everything in the swarm's radius OR condense on one target &amp; inflict lethal damage/drain Vitae equal to Blood Potency<br /> - Armor effective against swarm damage only if covering the whole body, and even then only at half normal rating<br /> - Everyone else in the swarm's radius takes -2 penalty to all actions; may trigger Breaking Points for the entophobic<br /> - Taking damage reduces radius proportionally (take half damage, shrink to half size)<br /> - Non-area damage capped at 1 (normal) or 2 (Exceptional Success)<br /> - On any turn in which the swarm condenses, these caps double (max. 2 normal, 4 Exceptional); easier to squish a lot of tiny things when they're all tightly grouped together<br /> - Full damage from fire, sunlight, area attacks<br /> - Celerity &amp; Resilience work as normal<br /> - Vigor passive adds one yard of extra radius per dot; Vigor active adds to effective Blood Potency for that turn when condensing<br /> - Can't use Claws of the Unholy<br /> - Only one physical &amp;quot;active&amp;quot; effect per turn (<i>e.g.</i> if using Vigor active, can't use Celerity active)*<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> *Watsonian explanation: each of those tiny, gnashing bodies can't channel the power of the Curse as effectively as the vampire's &amp;quot;real&amp;quot; form, and/or the vampire's power is already taxed by independently coordinating so many moving parts at once.<br /> <br /> Doylist explanation: being a swarm already makes it very tough for most foes to cause you harm. It should be an overall buff, to reflect the XP spent on the Merit, but the combination of automatic lethal damage (Vigor active) + swarm immunity + preemption in case someone brought a grenade or a flamethrower (Celerity active) seems too much; pick two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a good ADAPTATION as you call it. I actually using demon swarm rules to deal with Animalism 3, building upnthe size (and so the damage) a dot per turn to represent the more and more animals coming (considering bigger animals as a separated source of damage if needed).<br /> <br /> Here the discussion broke up about the original write up in the text and whether it is referring to Vampire's Brawl+strenght or not.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion to adapt it make a lot of sense anyway. I could consider to use it to balance the power indeed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T03:01:41-07:00","id":1377917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377816#post1377816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tessie is correct that the ChroD book was printed well after the VTR book so swarm form was already well established and well known for the writers to take into account.<br /> If the VTR book were fully capable of being used on it's own then why does it not include stats for a dog, frog, raven, etc? That logic does not add up at all. If you are looking for an OFFICIAL, printed stat block for a &quot;swarm of vermin,&quot; then that is presented in the ChroD book.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know how I brought up that OPP <i>did</i> release a complementary resource <i>specifically for Vampire</i> that <i>does</i> include stats for a dog, frog, raven, etc? Because, you know, those stats were missing? And yet they did not include any sort of swarm or Size 0 animals, as if those weren't expected to be used?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-02T16:47:14-07:00","id":1378091,"title":"","content":"So by that logic if I want to use say a otter as my beast form skin then I just use my vampire stats? or is it just for swarm form? because why would I use anything different? I mean everything else stays static when I use Beast's skin why would I choose not to be a group of bats that can punch through a brick wall with just their bodies. I mean why be a wolf when I can be a swarm of rats and be just more powerful with a much higher upper limit that only takes 1 to 2 damage per hit against me. man Combat and everything would just be so much easier if I can just use my stats and not take any real damage. Yeah that's it why didn't they just make protean 3 just swarm form its so much better then anything else. I mean I could be a BP3 vamp and still be swinging for 10 to 15 dice of damage and really not be hit by anything except a flamethrower. fuck I would just remain in swarm form and juts be prince of the city at BP 1 because nothing could really do any damage to me and combat would be a breeze. surely that's what the writers intended for swarm form to make the character who took it so powerful that they can ruin the story tellers campaign. must be it. why else would they make it.<br /> <br /> I mean its not like the rules of the things that must be used are spelled out. I mean surely I should just use my own stats and become nigh unkillable. I mean its not like you would make up a stat block for a animal that wasn't in any of the books. surely they would devote page count for a swarm when not every one is going to get that merit. I mean they should. it completely breaks the power because you just use your own stats. despite saying that the only stat you would switch out is the speed stat adjusted for creature size. I mean it say clearly plain as fucking day just use the stats of the vampire despite Beast's skin not working that way at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T01:39:48-07:00","id":1378208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378091#post1378091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So by that logic if I want to use say a otter as my beast form skin then I just use my vampire stats? or is it just for swarm form? because why would I use anything different?</div> </div> </div> </div>Otter is probably size 2 so not allowed for Swarm Form (I don't know and it doesn't matter anyway).<br /> I don't really get this point: Swarm form is allowing you to take the form of a swarm of ALSO size 0 animals which with normal Beast's Skin you can't. Meaning: bugs, spiders, wasps. Which is another evidence that we are talking about two different powers application (Coming back to the sentence: ...you can INSTEAD become...). And that's why Swarm Form is specifying you are using Vampire Speed (Which, AGAIN, is: Strenght+Dexterity) and (vampire) strenght+brawl to attack. Swarm form is specyfing all and only what you can do...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378091#post1378091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean everything else stays static when I use Beast's skin why would I choose not to be a group of bats that can punch through a brick wall with just their bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>because you CANNOT punch through a brick wall as, as well and clearily defined in the merit description, the only things you can do are:<br /> <br /> 1. Moving at the vamprie speed scaled down for species factor<br /> 2. Spread over up your BP x 5 yards<br /> 3. inflict distracted condition<br /> 4. only taking a point, max 2, of harm from all no-area damage sources<br /> 5. Attack using strenght+ Brawl.<br /> <br /> Breaking doors and walls is a Strenght+Stamina roll which is not even an option. (bats/rats/wasps can't punch at all as not having hands, by the way)<br /> <br /> Furthermore, you could theoretically destroy a brick wall even with the stat suggested by Rathamus, which are Strenght 4 stamina 3 (more than an average vampire) + the discipline like Vigor and Resilence which are applicable as clearily stated also in Beast's Skin description. So this your point does not have any sense at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378091#post1378091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean why be a wolf when I can be a swarm of rats and be just more powerful with a much higher upper limit that only takes 1 to 2 damage per hit against me. man Combat and everything would just be so much easier if I can just use my stats and not take any real damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why to shape into a rat or a crow instead to be only a bear, having a base strenght of 6 plus Vigor? It seems very simple to understand to me: any animals has different prerogative: A wolf is good in hunting and running, a Bat or a crow can fly, a bear is good to fight, a swarm is what you use when you have to beat your enemy down.... You are not using your swarm form to stealth into an house. You are using your bat or rat form for that.... that's also why you have a number of different transformation ready equal to protean. You use them situationally....also you need to spend 2 more XP to acquire the swarm form which is almost another discipline....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378091#post1378091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that's it why didn't they just make protean 3 just swarm form its so much better then anything else. I mean I could be a BP3 vamp and still be swinging for 10 to 15 dice of damage and really not be hit by anything except a flamethrower. fuck I would just remain in swarm form and juts be prince of the city at BP 1 because nothing could really do any damage to me and combat would be a breeze. surely that's what the writers intended for swarm form to make the character who took it so powerful that they can ruin the story tellers campaign. must be it. why else would they make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again. First of all swarm form cost you 2 more xp which is almost a new discipline......is almost having protean 4. Also, you use different transformations for different situations. I do not have other words to say that. It honestly seems very clear why you are not always in Swarm Form. Same reason you are not always in your Bear form....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378091#post1378091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean its not like the rules of the things that must be used are spelled out. I mean surely I should just use my own stats and become nigh unkillable. I mean its not like you would make up a stat block for a animal that wasn't in any of the books. surely they would devote page count for a swarm when not every one is going to get that merit. I mean they should. it completely breaks the power because you just use your own stats. despite saying that the only stat you would switch out is the speed stat adjusted for creature size. I mean it say clearly plain as fucking day just use the stats of the vampire despite Beast's skin not working that way at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you aware that, 90% of vampires, have basic strenght+brawl lower than the pool suggested in Swarm of Vermin (strenght 4)?? Since you can also apply discipline as vigor (as WELL STATED in the Beast's Skin description) What are we talking about???<br /> <br /> Other point, as seems you are considering to use Swarm of vermin stat from CoD as Rathamus suggested: In that Stat block you are not even having a Brawl skill. So, if that was the purpose of the developer: what Strenght + Brawl are you using? The overall Bite pool of the Dogs guards? Ok. Go for it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: let's make some example: if I become a Swarm of Vermin you are using the Dogs guard stat (page 121 of CoS - not sure what are you using as brawl though as it's not stated). Now, what stat are you using if I become a swarm of Wasps? What if I become a swarm of rats (which are far bigger and stronger than wasps)? Can you state down these?<br /> For Best's Skin we have several animals example which you can use for similar animals, not for swarms though?<br /> Are you only using Swarm of Vermins as template? Well, ok, so why no direct reference it into the merit text? (Other than because it wasn't there at that time...)? make very sense that the developer said: you are a Vampire becoming a swarm, the strongest you are the stronger is the swarm. Also because a BP 10 vampire is a larger swarm than a BP 3 vampire, how do you keep it into account? Does a 50 yards swarm have the same damage of a 15 yards one? No sense at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-03-2020, 05:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T13:54:53-07:00","id":1378339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377917#post1377917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how I brought up that OPP <i>did</i> release a complementary resource <i>specifically for Vampire</i> that <i>does</i> include stats for a dog, frog, raven, etc? Because, you know, those stats were missing? And yet they did not include any sort of swarm or Size 0 animals, as if those weren't expected to be used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, and where do I find this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-03T14:24:41-07:00","id":1378353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378339#post1378339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooh, and where do I find this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Already brought up in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377469#post1377469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Here (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...FVgSqjmpo/edit</a>) is the word doc with animal stat which is not including any swarm template. I went through CoD book and I couldn't find any swarm template as well. Pls point us out where the stats for sucg swarm are. So far, for me they aren't anywhere, hence the book cannot refer to any of such strenght+brawl roll of such</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-04T18:51:31-07:00","id":1378649,"title":"","content":"It always amazes me how often this pattern repeats.<br /> <br /> Someone asks a question.<br /> <br /> They get an answer that abides by a RAW reading (even if RAI may be under debate)<br /> <br /> They spend pages arguing against the answer they themselves requested.<br /> <br /> Using Swarm Form stats instead of Vampire stats fits with the text (admittedly not the only possible reading, but it does fit the text). It also fixes your &quot;Swarm Form too OP&quot; problem. So why are you fighting so hard against having your question answered?<br /> <br /> I can only assume it wasn't actually a question so much as a statement you expected glorious applause and agreement for, in which case maybe you just shouldn't have posted a thread. Vampire has never been about perfect balance and parity between abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T01:59:15-07:00","id":1378700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1378649#post1378649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always amazes me how often this pattern repeats.<br /> <br /> Someone asks a question.<br /> <br /> They get an answer that abides by a RAW reading (even if RAI may be under debate)<br /> <br /> They spend pages arguing against the answer they themselves requested.<br /> <br /> Using Swarm Form stats instead of Vampire stats fits with the text (admittedly not the only possible reading, but it does fit the text). It also fixes your &quot;Swarm Form too OP&quot; problem. So why are you fighting so hard against having your question answered?<br /> <br /> I can only assume it wasn't actually a question so much as a statement you expected glorious applause and agreement for, in which case maybe you just shouldn't have posted a thread. Vampire has never been about perfect balance and parity between abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Usually arguing is something done by more than just one person. It means someone else is arguing back to your argumentations.<br /> <br /> More over, if you read the post, I'm more than happy to accept or &quot;discuss&quot; other interpretation and house rule, as I did with AmusedByIrony suggestion (which I've also stated I'd probably begin to use...).<br /> <br /> The point of all this debate was not about an interpretation or a suggestion but about two different way to read the power, saying it is exactly how the power is actually desgineg by RAW. That' why we were arguing. Something issuggesting how to modify it, something else is to state the power is designed to work another way.<br /> <br /> This is a forum so it does also make sense people are discussing on a topic, doesn't it? Free to skip it whether you find it annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-05T06:18:39-07:00","id":1378738,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure if one more voice will help but here I go.<br /> Firstly we have animal stats so let\u2019s get that out of the way <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1xMwKNrnxhEuCQjP1qStbxl-C4JIyRmT1D4FVgSqjmpo/\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...T1D4FVgSqjmpo/</a><br /> Second This is 15 xp worth of abilities so it should be about as useful as similarly priced builds, obviously this is subjective.<br /> Claws of the Unholy is not reliable since it requires you to frenzy, in this state you can be led into a trap easily so said elder probably has his plan for next time.<br /> I believe that by strict reading of the rules to cold start this combo costs 4 Vitae since you need to activate Predatory Aspect before you can activate Unnatural Aspect, as soon as frenzy starts the beast will spend 2 Vitae so the elder will know what he\u2019s up against then the player can spend the next 2 as he wishes.<br /> BP 3 is not some nobody, it is what a one hundred year old vampire is expected to have, an elder should know better than to underestimate someone that old, they have grounds to suspect your player\u2019s been a very bad boy.<br /> That elder is probably now going to destroy the character or coterie to save face and make sure this never happens again, this is not something I enjoy doing when I ST so I understand others not wanting to do it. Also it\u2019s not fun for most players to deal with.<br /> I believe you still need to drain the blood from the creature you wish to use for swarm form so insects and the like are off limits.<br /> I agree that the animals stats should be used but I\u2019m not sure what to do about health since there\u2019s more than one. I don\u2019t know if there\u2019s any official ruling on what happens if said animal dies but returning to your regular form with the damage seems reasonable.<br /> Finally you don\u2019t become an elder by taking risks, elder should have known better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:50:16-07:00","id":1380150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1377855#post1377855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross-posted from the &quot;Vampires vs. Werewolves!&quot; thread:<br /> <br /> On swarms: as much as I like the VtR:2nd corebook, I'd suggest that Onyx Path really nailed the mechanics of swarms more effectively in Demon (pg. 179) and in Beast (pg. 126). If I were running another Vampire game, I'd probably adapt Swarm Form to the following:<br /> <br /> - Radius is two yards per dot of Blood Potency<br /> - Speed is double normal; move in three dimensions; fit through any opening<br /> - Inflict one bashing damage per turn to everything in the swarm's radius OR condense on one target &amp; inflict lethal damage/drain Vitae equal to Blood Potency<br /> - Armor effective against swarm damage only if covering the whole body, and even then only at half normal rating<br /> - Everyone else in the swarm's radius takes -2 penalty to all actions; may trigger Breaking Points for the entophobic<br /> - Taking damage reduces radius proportionally (take half damage, shrink to half size)<br /> - Non-area damage capped at 1 (normal) or 2 (Exceptional Success)<br /> - On any turn in which the swarm condenses, these caps double (max. 2 normal, 4 Exceptional); easier to squish a lot of tiny things when they're all tightly grouped together<br /> - Full damage from fire, sunlight, area attacks<br /> - Celerity &amp; Resilience work as normal<br /> - Vigor passive adds one yard of extra radius per dot; Vigor active adds to effective Blood Potency for that turn when condensing<br /> - Can't use Claws of the Unholy<br /> - Only one physical &quot;active&quot; effect per turn (<i>e.g.</i> if using Vigor active, can't use Celerity active)*<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> *Watsonian explanation: each of those tiny, gnashing bodies can't channel the power of the Curse as effectively as the vampire's &quot;real&quot; form, and/or the vampire's power is already taxed by independently coordinating so many moving parts at once.<br /> <br /> Doylist explanation: being a swarm already makes it very tough for most foes to cause you harm. It should be an overall buff, to reflect the XP spent on the Merit, but the combination of automatic lethal damage (Vigor active) + swarm immunity + preemption in case someone brought a grenade or a flamethrower (Celerity active) seems too much; pick two.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We tried this approach in my game, and my player hated it. His comment was, &quot;It's a neat power I want to use, but it feels like I stop participating in the combat when I use it. I don't make any choices or do anything.&quot; After he said that we took a closer look at the Merit as written and went with the &quot;use the physical stats of the animal&quot; and we haven't had problems since then. It's a very neat and effective ability, but it's situationally effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:56:14-07:00","id":1380202,"title":"","content":"Makes sense otherwise it\u2019s better than Protein 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:41:44-07:00","id":1380358,"title":"","content":"I still want to point out that the premise breaks down when Swarm Form can be (and, imo, is at its best and most thematic when) used for animals that would not be represented through any stats. A swarm of flesh-eating wasps would be horrifying, but it can do fuck all except move around and be distracting because a single wasp can't be meaningfully represented through Attributes and Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T07:16:51-07:00","id":1380379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380358#post1380358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want to point out that the premise breaks down when Swarm Form can be (and, imo, is at its best and most thematic when) used for animals that would not be represented through any stats. A swarm of flesh-eating wasps would be horrifying, but it can do fuck all except move around and be distracting because a single wasp can't be meaningfully represented through Attributes and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean you could just stat it out. The VtR core book had no stats for any animal so you have had to do it yourself. Its most likely why they never had a swarm form stat block. I swarm of rats is going to do more damage or being to move more things then say a swarm of mosquitos but you could turn into a swarm of rats or a swarm of mosquitos. so just talk to your ST and come up with some stats for whatever animal you want to make into a swarm.<br /> <br /> Its a static versus growth argument. If swarm can grow based on vamp stats why would I use anything but that after I pass the physical stats of a single large animal. I mean why use a bear if I can get the same amount of a swarm of insects and take less damage and cause a tilt. It would make no sense what so ever. but if you have a static swarm from suddenly you have a choice. Do I turn into the bear for the damage or do I turn into the swarm for defense and causing the tilt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T07:43:07-07:00","id":1380381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380358#post1380358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want to point out that the premise breaks down when Swarm Form can be (and, imo, is at its best and most thematic when) used for animals that would not be represented through any stats. A swarm of flesh-eating wasps would be horrifying, but it can do fuck all except move around and be distracting because a single wasp can't be meaningfully represented through Attributes and Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck drinking the wasps blood to enable you to change into one (or many as the case may be).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T08:55:34-07:00","id":1380387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380381#post1380381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good luck drinking the wasps blood to enable you to change into one (or many as the case may be).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you just have to consume the wasp. so just eating it would work I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:34:35-07:00","id":1380393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380379#post1380379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean you could just stat it out. The VtR core book had no stats for any animal so you have had to do it yourself. Its most likely why they never had a swarm form stat block. I swarm of rats is going to do more damage or being to move more things then say a swarm of mosquitos but you could turn into a swarm of rats or a swarm of mosquitos. so just talk to your ST and come up with some stats for whatever animal you want to make into a swarm.<br /> <br /> Its a static versus growth argument. If swarm can grow based on vamp stats why would I use anything but that after I pass the physical stats of a single large animal. I mean why use a bear if I can get the same amount of a swarm of insects and take less damage and cause a tilt. It would make no sense what so ever. but if you have a static swarm from suddenly you have a choice. Do I turn into the bear for the damage or do I turn into the swarm for defense and causing the tilt?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can surpass a bear with your regular stats, why take bear form at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T09:49:50-07:00","id":1380397,"title":"","content":"By the way, disciplines like Vigor are applied to Beast's Skin also. If you have not Blood Potency at 6 I doubt you can have raw Strenght (without vigor) at 6 (Bear stat). A Bear has also other stat like stamina which is quite high as well, meaning more health.<br /> And again, different teansformation are best fitting to different situation.<br /> <br /> But yes, if you already have Strenght 6 stamina 5, you do not need to get Bear's shape if not for the claw bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380381#post1380381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good luck drinking the wasps blood to enable you to change into one (or many as the case may be).</div> </div> </div> </div>As for any other size 0 animal. You just need to devoure it otherwise you can't become any size 0 animal at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T10:39:09-07:00","id":1380416,"title":"","content":"A mouse has blood, a wasp doesn\u2019t. The only example of a swarm given is rats so a Story Teller is free to say you can\u2019t become anything without blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:30:31-07:00","id":1380431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380416#post1380416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mouse has blood, a wasp doesn\u2019t. The only example of a swarm given is rats so a Story Teller is free to say you can\u2019t become anything without blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mouse is size 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:51:14-07:00","id":1380436,"title":"","content":"For all intents and purposes hemolymph is blood. The biological distinction shouldn't matter for a supernatural curse. I certainly wouldn't gain any Vitae from such a small amount, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-11-2020, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:20:03-07:00","id":1380441,"title":"","content":"Ok I\u2019ll accept that argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:09:05-07:00","id":1380529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380393#post1380393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you can surpass a bear with your regular stats, why take bear form at all?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean I don't anyone is going argue that a elder can take out a bear no problem. But once again its static vs. growth. A bear jaws can easily break bones and rend flesh, a rat bite cannot break bones and the most you have to worry about a rat bite or even a good amount of rat bites is the risk of infection. Even a good size swarm of rats would take a long time to kill someone(like all night according to one mobster who said he would tie people up in a cave and let rats eat the victim alive, though he was also a pathological liar who may have been making things up.) So how many rats or wasps or bats or whatever are you turning into here? 50? a hundred? A thousand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:14:13-07:00","id":1380531,"title":"","content":"Plus not being a bear is an easy alibi to arrange. I don\u2019t think anyone\u2019s ever gone to jail because they were mistaken for a bear in the modern age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T18:55:52-07:00","id":1380541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380529#post1380529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thousand?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite possibly. The swarm is measured in volume, not density or quantity, and the number of animals seem to be enough to fill that volume. Each individual specimen seem to be quite ephemeral. Those that leave the area rapidly die and decompose while leaving the vampire unharmed, while shooting into the swarm and damaging (not necessarily even killing) one of them does deal damage (though heavily diminished). Another reason why I think the Swarm Form is a representation of the vampire rather than a fully physical transformation to a swarm of critters. Just like Primeval Miasma is a physical representation of the vampire rather than a literal cloud of gas.<br /> The vampire isn't really the collection of all critters in the swarm; the vampire is the swarm and the critters are just the medium, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point about the bear is that once you surpass the bear in swarm form (at least when it comes to dice pools) you've already surpassed it in your regular form and is better served not taking that form at all, except when situationally appropriate. Saying that my interpretation of Swarm Form would makes the bear form obsolete ignores the fact that the bear form would've already have been made obsolete by your regular form (and you can still get claws/jaws through the cheaper Predatory Aspect, on top of being able to use weaponry). Not that it's much of a problem since Swarm Form is a development of Beast's Skin. It's kinda like saying the claws from Unnatural Aspect makes the claws from Predatory Aspect obsolete, which is certainly not a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-11-2020, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:30:04-07:00","id":1380565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380541#post1380541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite possibly. The swarm is measured in volume, not density or quantity, and the number of animals seem to be enough to fill that volume. Each individual specimen seem to be quite ephemeral. Those that leave the area rapidly die and decompose while leaving the vampire unharmed, while shooting into the swarm and damaging (not necessarily even killing) one of them does deal damage (though heavily diminished). Another reason why I think the Swarm Form is a representation of the vampire rather than a fully physical transformation to a swarm of critters. Just like Primeval Miasma is a physical representation of the vampire rather than a literal cloud of gas.<br /> The vampire isn't really the collection of all critters in the swarm; the vampire is the swarm and the critters are just the medium, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the point about the bear is that once you surpass the bear in swarm form (at least when it comes to dice pools) you've already surpassed it in your regular form and is better served not taking that form at all, except when situationally appropriate. Saying that my interpretation of Swarm Form would makes the bear form obsolete ignores the fact that the bear form would've already have been made obsolete by your regular form (and you can still get claws/jaws through the cheaper Predatory Aspect, on top of being able to use weaponry). Not that it's much of a problem since Swarm Form is a development of Beast's Skin. It's kinda like saying the claws from Unnatural Aspect makes the claws from Predatory Aspect obsolete, which is certainly not a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>By Raw that's not how the discipline or the merit works.<br /> The Beast's skin<br /> Her flesh ripples and warps as the vampire takes on the form<br /> of an animal. She must have consumed the beast \u2014 killing it<br /> by feeding from it. She can only take on the form of predatory<br /> animals, carrion-eaters, plague-carrying beasts, and parasites<br /> between Size 1 and 7. A vampire can keep a number of forms<br /> ready equal to her dots in Protean; to add or replace one she<br /> must consume the appropriate beast then slumber for a full day<br /> and night in her Unmarked Grave.<br /> <b>In animal form, she takes on the beast\u2019s Physical Attributes<br /> and Skills, and its Size, Speed, and Health</b>. She can move and<br /> sense and attack in any way that the animal can \u2014 a shark can<br /> swim and bite and sense blood, while a rat can scurry and bite,<br /> and a crow can fly. She may be unable to use some Physical<br /> Merits at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion. She can remain in her<br /> animal form indefinitely, but she still feels the need for blood<br /> burning within her, and sunlight still harms her.<br /> <br /> While in animal form, the vampire can use her Disciplines<br /> as normal.<br /> <br /> When taking the Beast\u2019s Skin, some Gangrel can<br /> instead become a swarm of small creatures: Size 0 or Size 1<br /> animals. The character may perceive through any of the senses<br /> <br /> of any individual creature in the swarm, but the swarm acts as<br /> a single entity.<br /> The swarm may spread over five yards or meters per dot of<br /> Blood Potency. Creatures beyond that range die and rapidly<br /> decompose. T<b>he swarm moves at the vampire\u2019s Speed, modified<br /> for the creatures\u2019 Size, in any logical direction.</b><br /> The swarm limits visibility and hearing, and causes panic in<br /> all those present. Everyone within the swarm\u2019s area suffers the<br /> persistent Distracted Condition (see p.302) until they get away.<br /> With Storyteller discretion, a swarm may have other features<br /> suited to the swarm animal. For example, rats should be better<br /> at biting through barricades.<br /> The swarm resists most harm. Roll attacks against the swarm<br /> as normal, but after factoring armor and other modifiers, the<br /> swarm only takes one point of damage of the appropriate type at<br /> most, or two points of damage with an exceptional success. Fire,<br /> sunlight, explosions, and other large-scale threats cause normal<br /> harm to the swarm, which is affected by banes as normal. To<br /> attack those within her swarm, roll Strength + Brawl, ignoring<br /> Defense. Divide the damage however you wish among those<br /> inside. Apply a victim\u2019s armor to the damage normally. The<br /> damage is lethal (bashing to Kindred). Alternately, a success<br /> may instead allow the vampire to take one Vitae from a victim.<br /> <br /> The only thing that would change from one to the next is you use the vampire's speed instead of the creature. You would need to stat out a swarm form based on what ever animal you are using. a swarm of rats is going to do different things then a swarm of crows or a swarm of bugs and will likewise have a different set of stats. So for a swarm of rats I might have slightly increased strength then just one but no matter how big the swarm I can't use it to punch through a wall. unlike a bear that can break bones with one bite or push down a tree. yes eventually a supernatural strong vampire will be able to surpass a bear even one that can use physical disciplines but a group of rats shouldn't be able to.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T04:49:22-07:00","id":1380619,"title":"","content":"I think that's an overly literal reading. You can't just take the stats of a single critter and apply it to the entire swarm because that's just ridiculous for a number of reasons. Compensating by adding dots makes sense but that is instead completely arbitrary or would require guidelines that doesn't exist to make it consistent. Not to mention that several possible swarms does not have stats in the first place. No, I'm not talking about animals that hasn't been written; I'm talking about animals that cannot be represented through Attributes and Skills, like basically all bugs.<br /> Using the vampire's own stats is the only solution I can imagine is intended because nothing else available at the time makes sense. We did get rules specifically for a swarm, but unlike the animal statblock document that was written and released specifically for Vampire, we got it much later in a book for a different game that has to be bought. It can be used, but it's neither RAW nor the intention of the writer at the time.<br /> <br /> Edit: And to be honest, if I want a vampire to turn into a roiling mass of worms or maggots, it would seriously help if they could actually do anything at all (other than moving with a relatively insane Speed and be mildly distracting).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 04-12-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:07:55-07:00","id":1380639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380619#post1380619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's an overly literal reading. You can't just take the stats of a single critter and apply it to the entire swarm because that's just ridiculous for a number of reasons. Compensating by adding dots makes sense but that is instead completely arbitrary or would require guidelines that does't exist to make it consistent. Not to mention that several possible swarms does not have stats in the first place. No, I'm not talking about animals that hasn't been written; I'm talking about animals that cannot be represented through Attributes and Skills, like basically all bugs.<br /> Using the vampire's own stats is the only solution I can imagine is intended because nothing else available at the time makes sense. We did get rules specifically for a swarm, but unlike the animal statblock document that was written and released specifically for Vampire, we got it much later in a book for a different game that has to be bought. It can be used, but it's neither RAW nor the intention of the writer at the time.<br /> <br /> Edit: And to be honest, if I want a vampire to turn into a roiling mass of worms or maggots, it would seriously help if they could actually do anything at all (other than moving with a relatively insane Speed and be mildly distracting).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I just use the Vampire 2e core book I get no animal stat block which means if I want to use the beast's skin or one of my player wants to use the beasts skin I have to make the physical skills and attributes. Thats what the beats skin says, so it would make sense that I would have to do that for swarm form itself because once again even different types of swarms are going to have different stats. it take a lot more force to kill a rat then it does a bug, a mosquito bite isn't going to do as much damage as a rats, a swarm of wasps aren't going to go faster then a swarm of bats, That just makes sense. So yeah if you want to use a vampire stats for swarm form go right ahead if thats easier for you but realize no where in the text does it say use the vampires stats for the swarm other than for speed and even that is adjusted for the size of the animal.<br /> <br /> Also yes different form are going to be for different uses. I would use a blood hound before I would use a bat to track something, a swarm can used used for multiple things that don't have to deal with combat. To get into places that even a size one animal would have problems with for instance, Scouting multiple locations is another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:35:09-07:00","id":1380646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grimmi05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op?p=1380639#post1380639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I just use the Vampire 2e core book I get no animal stat block which means if I want to use the beast's skin or one of my player wants to use the beasts skin I have to make the physical skills and attributes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's one way to fix it which is fine, but it's demonstrably not intended for anyone to have to come up with complete statblocks for Beast's Skin because they released animals as a free resource to complement the Vampire 2e core book specifically because animals were missing. It does not cover all animals, but it covers enough that it's possible to adjust for similar animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T07:27:13-07:00","id":1380650,"title":"","content":"Exactly, so if you are aware of it you would just scale up ro down a little bit. but if you are unaware such a resource exist then you would have to. Once again no where in the text does it say replace the physical skills and attributes with the vampires other then speed. If that's what they intended they would have said so because why make a exception for speed? the text would just read like &quot;Become a swarm of size 0 or 1 animals use the vampires skills and attributes&quot; you know like they did with protean 5 when you &quot;bite&quot; with your normal physical skills and attributes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T09:53:59-07:00","id":1380684,"title":"","content":"Note that Speed is modified by the chosen animal. That makes it an exception regardless of interpretation.<br /> It being clarified in Primeval Miasma isn't indicative of anything since Swarm Form was most likely written at a different stage in the process and quite possibly by a different writer. Unfortunately OPP is one of the worst RPG publishers I know of when it comes to editing (right now I can only think of Cubicle 7 and their take on WFRP as being worse). CofD books are great because of their amazing writers, and driven and experienced developers, but also incredibly sloppy at times (you know, like not including animals in the book where two out of ten core powers revolve around animals). I might be a bit quick to assume it sometimes, but I'm no longer surprised whenever it turns out what's written in the books doesn't reflect how it was intended to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:24:40-07:00","id":1380695,"title":"","content":"Yeah I agree, though they seem to be getting slightly better at it nowadays. That being said you either have to go by RAW or house rule it. Until a developer comes in and clarifies the ruling or does a ReRAW you really can't go by RAI because you don't know what they intended, you can only really guess which just leads to making a house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:32:48-07:00","id":1380712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1376957-swarm-form-too-op#post1376957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can a Gangrel in Swarm Form be handled. I mean, without flamethrower, granades, &quot;pesticides&quot;. It happened a frenzied Gangrel in my quest attacjed a BP 6 Elder, with tons of disciplines and it resulted in the Elder run away in front of a BP 3, relatively young vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without more details on the context, this sounds like a failure of planning more than anything. What was the larger context of this encounter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Swarm you are applying all your physical discipline and stats, </div> </div> </div>In Swarm Form you are specifically becoming a bunch of animals potentially smaller than the normal lower limit for the Discipline power the Merit requires. The only physical Discipline a character with the capacity to learn Protean naturally has affinity for is Resilience, and even with affinity you still have to buy Disciplines separately.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ignoring defense and you just receive 1 (max 2) damages per attack. In frenzy you even cannot be affected from mental discipline. </div> </div> </div>Without further context, I have no idea what options were available to the character that prompted this discussion, but I will also point out that banes still apply to the swarm and that lashing out is specifically a thing the Beast still engages with and that elders have a direct advantage in the ensuing conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, with Claws of Unholy are you still supposed to deal aggravated whil in Swarm? </div> </div> </div>Odds point to no, because most things that are Size 0 or 1 do not have claws capable of dealing even lethal damage to mortals. Common sense suggests that a power designed to make &quot;a near-master of Protean can manifest shredding claws that ignore armor and hit like a machete&quot; into &quot;this character's version of such claws hits less hard for more severe damage when they're frenzied, and in fact they always have to drop a Vitae to manifest these claws whenever they frenzy&quot; does not allow them to turn their separate modification of &quot;turn into an animal you've killed by feeding from it&quot; power from &quot;turn into a swarm of even smaller animals&quot; into &quot;turn into what is functionally a blob of extremely potent acid.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}